{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>It shall be reckoned to that man bloodgilt.</b> Because in the time of the first man all living creatures were forbidden to him for food, for nothing was permitted to him except fruits, as it is written (Genesis 1:29): ״הנה נתתי לכם את כל עשב זורע זרע ואת כל העץ אשר בו פרי עץ״ — until they were liable to destruction in the generation of the Flood and were saved by the merit of Noah, and then they were permitted to him for food. Therefore it says here that whoever slaughters within the camp or outside the camp and has not brought it first to the entrance of the Tent of Meeting — דם יחשב לאיש ההוא דם שפך, as though he had spilled human blood, for it reverts to its original prohibition that was in the time of the first man: he who slaughters an ox is like one who strikes a man. Thus Rashi explained."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:26:05.963983148Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}